2 CONT
2 CONT "William was Laird of Corse, a title given to his great-grandfather, a younger son of James, 2nd Lord Forbes. Castle Corse was not in Banchory but in an eponymous hamlet some 25 miles to the northwest. Their seat was reduced durin
2 CONC g the Commonwealth, and their burial place, the chapel kirkfield served the hamlet of Corse as Terry Chapel as long as any population remained. It is now in a scattered state, overgrown by a grove of trees. **
2 CONT His chart to JOHN ALDEN LINES: Abigail Byram
2 CONT her mother → Anna Alden
2 CONT her mother → Elizabeth Keith
2 CONT her mother → Deacon Edward Fobes
2 CONT her father → Col. John Forbes
2 CONT his father → Rev. John Forbes
2 CONT his father → William Forbes of Corse
2 CONT his father
2 CONT ***From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on William Forbes:
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p17647.htm#i176462
2 CONT William Forbes of Corse [1]
2 CONT M, #176462,
2 CONT d. 1596
2 CONT Last Edited=13 Jan 2010
2 CONT William Forbes of Corse was the son of Patrick Forbes of Corse and Marjory Lumsden.[2]
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Strachan, daughter of unknown Strachan of Thornton.[2]
2 CONT He died in 1596.[2]
2 CONT He lived at Corsse, Scotland.[1]
