2 CONT
2 CONT "The Rev Sir John Forbes was the brother of Patrick Forbes who established Presbyterian colonies in Ulster, and whose son John was a major theologian and apologist for that denomination. Rev Forbes tried to work within the Church 
2 CONC of Scotland, friendly to his faith and itself a bit contrarian to the High Anglican Church-- James I reached his limit with Ref Forbes and banished him to Holland, where our branch of the Forbes clan lived for a generation before 
2 CONC moving on to New England. Rev Forbes himself, however, reconciled with England and accepted a knighthood and priesthood in an Anglican church, presumably in Aberdeen where he died. He was the last of our family to be buried in the
2 CONC  Keig Kirkyard near Alford, now a ruined outbuilding on lands belonging to Castle Forbes. He was locally noted, and may still be, for murdering the man who haunts Craigievar Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Near present-day Castle Forbes."
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/70664690/john-forbes]
