2 ADDR
3 CITY Freie Reichstadt Hamburg
3 CTRY Heiliges Römisches Reich (Present Germany)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Captain Arthur Forbes, of Castle Forbes</strong>, in the parish of Clongish, co Longford, 6th son of William Forbes of Corse, by Elizabeth, daughter of (--) Strachen of Thornton, settled in Ireland in 1620, and was made a
2 CONC  free denizen thereof, 1 April 1622; received lands, in the counties of Leitrim and Longford, erected into the manor of Castle Forbes; and was created a Baronet [S] 29 September, sealed 10 October 1628, with rem. to heirs male wha
2 CONC tsoever, and with a grant of, presumably, 16,000 acres in Nova Scotia, of which he had seizin in November 1628. He was Colonel of a regiment in the service of Gustavus Adolphus, King of Sweden. He married, between 12 February 1618
2 CONC  and 1623, Jane, widow of Sir Claud Hamilton, of Clonyn, co Cavan, daughter of Robert Lauder, of the Bass [S]. He died 14 April 1632, being slain in a duel at Hamburgh. His widow suffered greatly in the Civil Wars, and was besiege
2 CONC d for many months at Castle Forbes till forced to surrender in August 1642."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n379/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 360
