1 OCCU Baron of Ochiltree, 2nd lord av Ochiltree, riddare, Överste i Edinburg Scotland, Hos Maria Stuart -med henne till Frankrike. Överste hos Frans II av Frankrike, 2nd Lord Stewart of Ochiltree, 2nd lord of Avondale
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Ochiltree''' (c. 1521–1591) fought for the Scottish Reformation. His daughter married John Knox and he played a part in the defeat of Mary, Queen of Scots at the battle of Langside.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===ANDREW STEWART, LORD OCHILTREE===
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.thepeerage.com/p2519.htm#i25183 '''thepeerage.com''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Stewart of Ochiltree was born after 1521. He was the son of Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Stewart of Ochiltree and Margaret Hamilton.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, firstly, Agnes Cuninghame, daughter of Sir John Cuninghame, 4th of Caprington, before 27 October 1549.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Lady Margaret Cuninghame, daughter of Alexander Cuninghame, 5th Earl of Glencairn and Lady Janet Hamilton, between August 1570 and February 1572/73.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 21 March 1601/2.4 [Wikipedia: Lord Ochiltree died in November 1591.[5]]
2 CONT
2 CONT He succeeded as the 2nd Lord Stewart of Ochiltree [S., 1543] in 1549.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Stewart of Ochiltree and Janet Forbes
2 CONT #John Stewart5
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Stewart of Ochiltree and Agnes Cuninghame
2 CONT
2 CONT # James Stewart, 1st and last Earl of Arran+4 d. 5 Dec 1595
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart, Master of Ochiltree+4 d. b 10 Sep 1578
2 CONT # Sir William Stewart+4 d. 1588
2 CONT # Henry Stewart+4
2 CONT # Robert Stewart of Pittheustes+4
2 CONT # Isabel Stewart4
2 CONT # Berthia Stewart4 [shows wrong husband]
2 CONT # Margaret Stewart4 b. c 1548, d. a 1612
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/512/mode/2up '''The Scots Peerage'''], Vol. 6, page 512-514:
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. '''ANDREW''' STEWART, second Lord Ochiltree, called, from his zeal for the reformed religion, ' the Good Lord,' born about 1521 ,8 succeeded his father. He early declared for the principles of the Reformation and was one of th
2 CONC e staunch supporters of Knox in 1555, and remained his friend through life. He opposed the marriage of Queen Mary and Darnley, and fled into England, but returned after the murder of Riccio, and was wounded, * sore hurt and in dan
2 CONC ger of his life . . . receiving his chief wound with a sword in his neck, given by the Lord Herris ' at the battle of Langside. He became a member of the Privy Council of King James vi., and one of the Lords of the Articles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In later life he was chiefly known as father of the King's favourite, James, Earl of Arrau, 'and some others of ill government. His own lyuinge and power of lyttle value.' 10 He died about 1592." He married, first, Agnes Cunningha
2 CONC m, who with him had a charter of Pennymore and others 27 March 1549. She was living 31 January 1556-57, when she is mentioned in a charter of lands in Ochiltree,12 and is stated to have been * filia domini de Oaprington.' 13 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, secondly, Margaret Cunyngham, widow of John Wallace of Oraigie, and daughter of Alexander, fourth Earl of Glencairn,1 who died in June 1573. Her testament dative was given up by the children of her first marriage, and 
2 CONC she is styled ‘ sometyme spous to ane Nobill Lord Andro Lord Stewart of Ochiltrie.' 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Ochiltree had issue : —
2 CONT * 1. '''ANDREW''', Master of Ochiltree, of whom presently. … He married, before 9 March 1566-67,1 Margaret Stewart, daughter of Henry, second Lord Methven
2 CONT * 2. '''''James''''' Stewart,3 the favourite of the young King James vi., created Earl of Arran. (See that title.) had issue .. 
2 CONT * 3. '''''Sir William Stewart''''' of Monkton … He married Helen Ouningham, relict of John Stewart, burgess of Ayr, .. had issue … 
2 CONT * 4. '''''Henry Stewart''''' of Barskimming and Gogar, son lawful, …  Married about 1580, Janet, second daughter of Adam Reid of Barskimming,2 and had issue …
2 CONT * 5. '''''Robert Stewart''''' of Pittheveles, also designed of Halltoun of Limcartie. In 1609 he obtained a grant of 2000 acres in Ulster/ Married (contract 1586) Jean Ross, daughter of John Ross of Oraigie,5 whose testament was r
2 CONC ecorded 14 February 1601 …
2 CONT * 6. '''''Isabel''''', stated to have been married to Thomas Kennedy of Bargany.9
2 CONT * 7. '''''Margaret'''''. Married, first, when a young girl, March 1564, to the elderly Reformer, Mr. John Knox. She was married, secondly (contract dated 8 January 1573-74 "), to Sir Andrew Ker of Faldonside. She was still alive i
2 CONC n 1598 or 1599.12
2 CONT * 8. '''''Bethia'''''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stewart-1647
2 CONT
2 CONT He also had two natural children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth Stewart, legitimated 31 March 1585[1]
2 CONT # John Stewart (with Janet Forbes)[5] (for Stuarts in Sweden see Hans Stuart (abt.1550-1618))
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart died after 3 June 1596.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stewart,_2nd_Lord_Ochiltree Wikipedia] Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Ochiltree
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish connection
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew 2nd Lord Ochiltree seems to have had a son with Janet Forbes, John Stewart or Stuart. He entered the service of Sweden and was master of horse to Eric XIV,[20] and had two sons Andrew and John. This branch of the Ochiltree 
2 CONC family is introduced at the Swedish House of Lords (Riddarhuset) under the name Stuart. Hans (Johannes) Stuart (d. 1618) obtained a letter of descent in Edinburgh in 1579 and a letter of arms at Holyrood Castle in Edinburgh from K
2 CONC ing James VI of Scotland in 1585 [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Stuart married Brita Eriksdotter Soop, and their daughter Martha Stuart (1606-1653) married a French lieutenant-colonel, Anton Ydron, who was killed at the battle of Nürnberg in 1632 in the Thirty Years' War (1618–48). As a w
2 CONC idow Martha Stuart lived on the island of Almö, and was a frequent correspondent of the Swedish chancellor, Axel Oxenstierna, whose castle Tidö Slott was nearby.[21]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From Wikipedia''': Lord Ochiltree (or Ochiltrie) of Lord Stuart of Ochiltree was a title in the Peerage of Scotland. In 1542 Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Avondale (see the Earl Castle Stewart for earlier history of the family) exch
2 CONC anged the lordship of Avondale with Sir James Hamilton for the lordship of Ochiltrie and by Act of Parliament was ordained to be styled Lord Stuart of Ochiltrie. His great-grandson, the third Lord Stuart of Ochiltrie, resigned the
2 CONC  feudal barony of Ochiltree and the peerage to his cousin, Sir James Stuart, with the consent of the Crown in 1615. In 1619 he was instead elevated to the Peerage of Ireland as Baron Castle Stewart; see the Earl Castle Stewart for
2 CONC  further history of this branch of the family. Sir James Stuart now became the first or fourth Lord Ochiltrie (or Lord Stuart of Ochiltrie). He was succeeded by his son William, the second or sixth Lord. On his early death in 1675
2 CONC  the lordship became either dormant or extinct.
2 CONT
2 CONT A branch of the Ochiltree family is introduced at the Swedish House of Lords (Riddarhuset) under the name Stuart. Hans (Johannes) Stuart (d. 1618) obtained a letter of descent in Edinburgh in 1579 and a letter of arms at Holyrood 
2 CONC Castle in Edinburgh from King James VI of Scotland in 1585.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lords Ochiltree''' (1542)
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Ochiltree (c. 1505–1548)
2 CONT # Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Ochiltree (c. 1521–1591)
2 CONT # Andrew Stuart, 3rd Lord Ochiltree (c. 1560–1629) (resigned lordship in 1615 and created Baron Castle Stewart in 1619)
2 CONT # James Stewart, 4th Lord Ochiltree (1595–c. 1658)
2 CONT # William Stewart, 5th Lord Ochiltree (c. 1659–1675)
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stewart,_2nd_Lord_Avondale]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Title''':  Andrew's father was the 1st Lord Avondale of a new creation, Andrew surrendered his title for a new investment as Lord Ochiltree. His seat became Ochiltree Castle in Ayrshire. The original Avondale lands were purchas
2 CONC ed or exchanged with James Hamilton of Finnart. He exchanged his lands at East Wemyss (which came from his wife or father) with Ochiltree, which belonged to the Comptroller, James Colville. In August 1534, Finnart made the exchang
2 CONC e with Lord Avondale for the barony of Avandale.[1] Andrew was confirmed as Lord Avondale by Regent Arran, Finnart's half-brother, on 12 March 1543.[2]
2 CONT '''Activities''' : Andrew attended Parliaments in 1524 and 1525. When James V first assumed power by escaping from the Douglas family and joining his mother at Stirling Castle, Avondale was one of eight lords and earls who came to
2 CONC  advise them. Margaret Tudor noted they had not kept court since the murder of the Earl of Lennox in 1526. Avondale also accompanied James to Edinburgh in July 1528, and attended the September parliament.[3]
2 CONT 'Lord Ochiltree,' probably Andrew, sat on the trial that condemned Janet Douglas, Lady Glamis for treason on 8 July 1537.[4]
2 CONT '''Family''': Andrew first [secondly] married Margaret Hamilton,[5] and secondly [firstly] Agnes Cunningham of the Caprington family; their children included Margaret who married John Knox and the soldier and politician James, who
2 CONC  became Earl of Arran and dominated Scottish politics after the Ruthven regime until his fall in 1585.
2 CONT '''Brothers''': Andrew's brother was created Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Methven on his marriage to the King's mother Margaret Tudor. Another brother James was made Captain of Doune Castle and Forester of Glenfinglas and Menteith on 1
2 CONC 4 July 1528.[6] James's son became James Stewart, 2nd Earl of Moray.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Notes''': John Stuart, son of Andrew Stewart (Stuart) of Ochiltree and Brita (Beatrix?) Douglas. John was a Knight, he followed Mary Stuart to France where he became a colonel in King Frans II's regiment of infantry, returned t
2 CONC o Scotland (Edinburgh) in 1560. He was married to Agneta (Agnes?) Forbes, daughter of Robert Forbes and Anna Sinclaire. John had 2 sons, John and Andrew (in swedish the where called Hans and Anders) who emigrated to Sweden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
