1 NAME Janet /Forbes/ Countess of Atholl
2 GIVN Janet
2 SURN Forbes
2 NSFX Countess of Atholl
2 _MARNM Forbes
1 SEX F
1 TITL Lady
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == LADY JANET FORBES Countess of Atholl ==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Janet Forbes, here treated, is the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/John-Forbes-6th-Lord-Forbes/6000000002116086456?through=6000000008630790120 and his third wife https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Barlow/6000000
2 CONC 006444780187?through=6000000008630790120 She had a charter for part of Balquhain from John Leslie of Balquhain on 9 January 1547-48. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/55/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 55
2 CONC ]'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == First Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Janet Forbes, here treated, married,  first in 1542, to John Stewart, third Earl of Atholl. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/55/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 55]'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Second Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Janet Forbes, here treated married, secondly, to Alexander Hay of Delgaty. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/55/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 55]'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Third Marriage ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lady Janet Forbes, here treated, married,  thirdly, to William Lesly of Balquhain. [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/55/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 55]'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 January 1550: Charter by which John Leslie of Boquhane confirms that he has given part of the lands of Syde in the Regality of Garreauch and sheriffdom of Aberdeen, to his son William Leslie, and William's wife Jonete Forbes
2 CONC . William and Jonete were to hold this land in conjunct fee and liferent, and it was to pass to their lawful male heirs, whom failing to the nearest heirs whatsoever of John Leslie of Boquhane. This charter was confirmed under the
2 CONC  Great Seal of Scotland on 8 April 1554. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/210/mode/1up RMS 1546-80: charter number 941]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi04scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1546-1580. Edited by John Maitland Thomson, MA., Advocate. (H. M. Gen
2 CONC eral Register House, Edinburgh, 1886), 1180 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=John_Forbes,_6th_Lord_Forbes&oldid=1257851784  John Forbes, 6th Lord Forbes] (died 1547) was a Scottish landowner. He was the son of William Forbes, 3rd Lord Forbes and Christian Gordon,
2 CONC  daughter of Alexander Gordon, 1st Earl of Huntly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Forbes' third wife was Elizabeth Berlay, widow of Lord Elphinstone. Their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Arthur Forbes of Putachie, known as "Black Arthur", who was killed at the battle of Tillieangus in October 1571.
2 CONT #Jean or Janet Forbes, who married (1) John Stewart, 3rd Earl of Atholl, (2) Alexander Hay of Delgatie, (3) William Leslie of Balquhain.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT #James Balfour Paul,'' Scots Peerage,'' vol. 4 (Edinburgh, 1907), p. 53. < [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/52/mode/2up Archive.Org] > 
2 CONT # Matthew Lumsden, Genealogy of the Family of Forbes (Inverness, 1819), p. 12. < [https://books.google.com/books?id=sZdDAAAAYAAJ&pg=PP13&source=kp_read_button&hl=en&newbks=1&newbks_redir=0#v=onepage&q&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT # '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft/page/55/mode/1up The Scots Peerage IV: 55]'''
2 CONT # '''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stewart,_2nd_Lord_Ochiltree?wprov=sfti1 Wikipedia]'''
