1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johan_Adolph_Stuart '''Johan Adolf Stuart'''], född 1 juni 1603 i Dorpat, död 30 april 1666 i Vists församling, Östergötlands län, var en svensk adelsman och militär
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johan Adolf Stuart''' föddes 1603 i Dorpat. Han var son till översten [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anders_Stuart_den_%C3%A4ldre '''Anders Stuart''' den äldre] och Elisabeth Anrep. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stuart blev''' 1626 fänrik vid Östgöta regemente till fot, 1628 kapten och 1631 regementskvartermästare. Han blev slutligen överstelöjtnant och kommendant på [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannisborg Johannisborg]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stuart och hans''' fru avstod arvsanspråket 12 januari 1659 efter hennes broder Anders Stuart. Stuart avled 1666 på [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stavs%C3%A4ter Stavsäter] i Vists församling och begravdes i Vists kyrka.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Egendom===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stuart ägde''' gården [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stavs%C3%A4ter Stavsäter] i Vists socken.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Familj===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stuart gifte sig''' 1633 med sin kusin '''Anna Stuart''' (död 1670), dotter till generalmönsterherren Hans Stuart och Brita Eriksdotter Soop. Stuart gifte sig mot sina föräldrars samtycke och fick enligt kungliga senatens beslu
2 CONC t 15 april 1633 böta till Linköpings domkyrka.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Vapen==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Heraldic Analysis of the Stuart Coat of Arms===
2 CONT ​
2 CONT The image is a quarterly shield, which is a traditional way of combining several lineages or titles into a single coat of arms. It accurately reflects the complex history of the House of Stewart (Stuart).
2 CONT ​
2 CONT Breakdown of the Quarters
2 CONT ​
2 CONT First Quarter (Top Left): This features the Royal Arms of Scotland. It displays a red lion rampant (standing on its hind legs) within a red "double tressure flory-counter-flory" (the decorative border with fleurs-de-lis) on a gold
2 CONC  field. This represents the family’s long reign as Kings and Queens of Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ​Second Quarter (Top Right): This shows a gold field with a blue and silver checkered band (fess chequy). This is the original and most famous emblem of the High Stewards of Scotland. The checkered pattern is said to represent the
2 CONC  cloth used by the early Stewards for counting money in their role as royal treasurers.
2 CONT ​
2 CONT Third Quarter (Bottom Left): This depicts a red diagonal cross (saltire) between four red roses on a silver field. This is the coat of arms of the House of Lennox. The Stuart of Lennox branch was a major cadet branch; notably, Lor
2 CONC d Darnley (Mary Queen of Scots' husband) belonged to this line.
2 CONT ​
2 CONT Fourth Quarter (Bottom Right): This displays a gold lion rampant on a red field. This is the traditional arms of the Earldom of Fife, an ancient Scottish title that became linked to the Stewarts through marriage and inheritance.
2 CONT
2 CONT ​Conclusion
2 CONT
2 CONT ​The image is a very faithful representation of a high-ranking member of the Stuart dynasty. Rather than being a simple family crest, it is a compositional shield that tells the story of the family's rise to royalty and their stra
2 CONC tegic alliances with other powerful Scottish noble houses.
