2 CONC branch owned from the end of the 14th century to into the 16th century Ugglebo in Ryssby sn (Kronob.). The genealogy of the family, which was already disputed in an inheritance process in 1475, is nowhere fully satisfactorily inve
2 CONC stigated; its weapon was a dragon. It has been stated, but without binding evidence, that from this family would possibly descend the noble family, which was introduced in 1646 and then became called Drake af Torp and Hamra (proba
