1 NAME Andrew /Stewart/ Master of Ochiltree
2 GIVN Andrew
2 SURN Stewart
2 NSFX Master of Ochiltree
2 _MARNM Stewart
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1535
2 ADDR
3 CITY Atholl
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 10 SEP 1578
2 ADDR
3 CITY Postcarrick
3 STAE Scotland
1 OCCU Governor of Edinburgh Castle
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Predeceased his father, therefore was '''never''' "Lord Ochiltree". His son, another Andrew, became 3rd Lord Ochiltree instead, and then 1st Baron Castle Stuart.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.thepeerage.com/p2501.htm#i25005
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, Master of Ochiltree was the son of Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Stewart of Ochiltree and Agnes Cunningham.2 He married Margaret Stewart, daughter of Henry Stewart, 2nd Lord Methven and Jean Ruthven, before 9 March 1566
2 CONC /67.1 He died before 10 September 1578.     He was styled as Master of Ochiltree
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/GEN-MEDIEVAL/2013-11/1384903637 Is President JFK a Plantagenet Descendant ? ] Nov 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, Master of Ochiltree, and his wife Margaret Stewart of Methven, did have a daughter who married a Gilbert Kennedy. But he was of a different Kennedy family, not the one shown in Tim Dowling's pedigree, and his line 
2 CONC died out with his Thomas who died sp.
2 CONT
2 CONT The account of Stewart of Ochiltree in vol. 6 of SP gives the following seven daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. Margaret, m. John Stewart of Traquair
2 CONT * 2. Anne, m. Andrew Ker, 1st Lord Jedburgh
2 CONT * 3. Marjory, m. Sir Roger Aston
2 CONT * 4. Martha, m. Nichol Rutherford of Hundalee
2 CONT * 5. Jean or Anna, m. Gilbert Kennedy, "apparent heir of Thomas Kennedy of Bargany"
2 CONT * 6. Agnes
2 CONT * 7. Susanna
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
