1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == ANDREW STEWART Lord Ochiltree ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Andrew Stewart: "third Lord  Avandale, and first Lord Ochiltree, is the son of the  last [Andrew Stewart, Lord Avondale]. He took the side, during the minority of King James V, of  the Queen-mother, who married  his brother, He
2 CONC nry, Lord Methven, and in 1525 he received a pardon for taking the field against the Regent, John, Duke of Albany. His affairs becoming involved, he exchanged his lands of Avandale with Sir James Hamilton of Pynnart for the lands 
2 CONC and barony of Ochiltree, and this transfer was confirmed by a charter under the Great  Seal on 2  September 1534. On 15 March 1542-43 an Act of  Parliament ordained him 'to be callit, he and his successiouris in tyme to cum, LORD 
2 CONC STEWART OF OYOHELTREE, and to haif vote and place in the parliament as utheris lordis of the realme aught and sould haif in ye  samin, haifand all honouris and dignities efferand thereto.'  He  and his successors thenceforth bore 
2 CONC the title of Lord Ochiltree, and he himself sometimes Lord Ochiltree and Failford. He died about1548, as next year his son appears as Lord Ochiltree. He married, before 22 August 1515, Margaret  Hamilton. She is styled 'fllia noth
2 CONC a' of James, Earl of  Arran, and was unquestionably one of his many illegitimate children. She had with her husband at that date confirmation of the lands of Glengevil." [https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page
2 CONC /511/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: pp. 511-12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''25 July 1531: Charter by which James V, King of Scots, confirms that he has given, with certain exceptions, the land and barony of Avandale in the sheriffdom of Lanark, to Andrew Stewart, son and apparent heir of Andrew, Lord A
2 CONC vandale. The barony had previously been resigned by Lord Avandale, who reserved his own liferent and the terce of his wife [ not named ]. [https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/229/mode/1up RMS 1513-46: charter n
2 CONC umber 1043]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Printed Evidence ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/registrummagnisi03scot/page/n6/mode/1up Registrum Magni Sigilli Regum Scotorum. The Register of the Great Seal of Scotland, A.D. 1513-1546. Edited by James Balfour Paul, FSA. Scot., and John Maitlan
2 CONC d Thomson, MA., Advocates. (H. M. General Register House, Edinburgh, 1883), 1067 pp. including indices and errata]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Genealogy ==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''[https://archive.org/details/scotspeeragefoun06pauluoft/page/511/mode/1up The Scots Peerage VI: pp. 511-12]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://thepeerage.com/p2518.htm#i25178 Biographical Summary from Darryl Lundy's Peerage] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Stewart of Ochiltree was the son of Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Avandale and Margaret Kennedy.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Margaret Hamilton, daughter of James Hamilton, 1st Earl of Arran and Beatrix Drummond, circa 22 August 1515.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1548.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Avandale [S., 1500] on 9 September 1513.[2] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Master Usher of the Kings Chamber in 1524.[2] 
2 CONT *He held the office of Sheriff of of Dunbartonshire in 1527.[2] 
2 CONT *He was created 1st Lord Stewart of Ochiltree [Scotland] on 15 March 1542/43, after exchanging his feudal barony of Avandale with Sir James Hamilton of Finnart for that of Ochiltree.[1],[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Andrew Stewart, 1st Lord Stewart of Ochiltree and Margaret Hamilton
2 CONT *1. Isabel Stewart [2]
2 CONT *2. Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Stewart of Ochiltree+[3] b. a 1521, d. 21 Mar 1601/2
2 CONT *3. Walter Stewart [2] b. a 1522
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stewart,_2nd_Lord_Avondale Biographical Summary from Wikipedia] ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Avondale or Andrew Stuart, 1st Lord Ochiltree, (died 1549), Scottish peer.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Title'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew's father was the 1st Lord Avondale of a new creation, Andrew surrendered his title for a new investment as Lord Ochiltree. His seat became Ochiltree Castle in Ayrshire. The original Avondale lands were purchased or exchange
2 CONC d with James Hamilton of Finnart. He exchanged his lands at East Wemyss (which came from his wife or father) with Ochiltree, which belonged to the Comptroller, James Colville. In August 1534, Finnart made the exchange with Lord Av
2 CONC ondale for the barony of Avandale.[1] Andrew was confirmed as Lord Avondale by Regent Arran, Finnart's half-brother, on 12 March 1543.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Activities'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew attended Parliaments in 1524 and 1525. When James V first assumed power by escaping from the Douglas family and joining his mother at Stirling Castle, Avondale was one of eight lords and earls who came to advise them. Marga
2 CONC ret Tudor noted they had not kept court since the murder of the Earl of Lennox in 1526. Avondale also accompanied James to Edinburgh in July 1528, and attended the September parliament.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Lord Ochiltree,' probably Andrew, sat on the trial that condemned Janet Douglas, Lady Glamis for treason on 8 July 1537.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew married Margaret Hamilton, a daughter of James Hamilton, 1st Earl of Arran,[5] Their children included Andrew Stewart, 2nd Lord Ochiltree father of Margaret who married John Knox, and the soldier and politician James, who b
2 CONC ecame Earl of Arran and dominated Scottish politics after the Ruthven regime until his fall in 1585. When Margaret married Knox in 1563, the marriage angered Mary, Queen of Scots, because she was of "the blood and name".[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Brothers'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew's brother was created Henry Stewart, 1st Lord Methven on his marriage to the King's mother Margaret Tudor. Another brother James was made Captain of Doune Castle and Forester of Glenfinglas and Menteith on 14 July 1528.[7] 
2 CONC James's son became James Stewart, 2nd Earl of Moray
2 CONT
2 CONT '''References'''
2 CONT
