1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Rehnski%C3%B6ld_nr_48
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Gustav_Rehnski%C3%B6ld
2 CONT
2 CONT Count Carl Gustav Rehnskiöld (6 August 1651 - 29 January 1722) was a Swedish Field Marshal under the command of King Charles XII of Sweden. Despite being choleric and irritable, Rehnskiöld's military skills made him the chief mili
2 CONC tary advisor and second-in-command to King Charles and earned him the epithet the "Parmenio of the Northern Alexander."
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Rehnskiöld was born in Stralsund as a son of Gerd Antoni Rehnskiöld and Birgitta Torskeskål.
2 CONT
2 CONT During his life, he played an important role in the Great Northern War. He commanded at the Battle of Fraustadt, after which King Charles XII made him a Field Marshal and Count. Highlights of his career include a highly successful
2 CONC  campaign against Poland from 1701-1703, and the disastrous Ukrainian campaign which ended with the Battle of Poltava in 1709. The Battle was a disaster for the Swedish army and Rehnskiöld was captured by the Russians. He remained
2 CONC  in Russian captivity until 1718.
