1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>William Keith, 4th Earl Marischal</strong> '''(d. 7 October 1581) was a Scottish nobleman and politician...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...'''William Keith was the son''' of Robert Keith, Master of Marischal and Lady Elizabeth Douglas, daughter of John Douglas, 2nd Earl of Morton. '''He succeeded his grandfather''', William Keith, 3rd Earl Marischal. '''He was one
2 CONC  of the earls who accompanied''' James V to France for his marriage to Madeleine of Valois, daughter of King Francis I of France. The wedding took place on 1 January 1537 at Notre Dame Cathedral in Paris and was followed by days o
2 CONC f Jousting at the Louvre...
2 CONT
2 CONT ...'''He was married to Margaret Keith''', eldest daughter of William Keith younger, of Inverugie, '''with whom he obtained large estates. He and Margaret had twelve children:
2 CONT * William Keith, Master of Marischal (died 1580).[8]
2 CONT * Hon. Robert Keith, 1st Lord Altrie (died 1596).[9]
2 CONT * John Keith, probable Rector of Duffas.[9]
2 CONT * Agnes Keith, Countess of Moray (or Annas), m. 1st to the Regent Moray, 2nd. to Colin Campbell, 6th Earl of Argyll. She died 16 July 1588 at Edinburgh.[9]
2 CONT * Alison, m. to Alexander Abernethy, 6th Lord Saltoun (died 1587).[9]
2 CONT * Mary, m. to Sir John Campbell of Calder (dispensation for consanguinity).[9]
2 CONT * Beatrice, m. to Sir John Allardice of Allardice. She died 19 May 1596.[9]
2 CONT * Joneta, m. to James Crichton of Frendraught.[9]
2 CONT * Margaret, m. to John Kennedy of Blairquhan.[9]
2 CONT * Elizabeth, m. to Sir Alexander Irvine of Drum.[9]
2 CONT * Isobel, m. Alexander Strachan of Thornton. She died August 1595.[9] Barbara, promised in m., failing her sister Isobel, to Alexander Strachan; m. Alexander Forbes of Pitsligo.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Keith's chief residence was Dunnottar Castle in Aberdeenshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''When he died on 7 October 1581, he was succeeded by his grandson''', George Keith, son of William, Master of Marischal; George became the 5th Earl Marischal."
2 CONT
