1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''Robert 'Lumsden, Lord of Maidler Cushnie, and secretary of state to James IV of Scotland.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1509 he received a charter of Cushnie in free barony from King James IV.1 He had 17 younger children.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lumsden,Lumisden,  Lumsdaine, Lumsdale family has ancient roots with charters starting in 1188.
2 CONT
2 CONT In older documents their name is sometimes spelled "Alomesdel". (Forbes, Leith, Vol. I, pp. 172, 175). Sir Walter Scott made use of a character named Lumsdale.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Burke's Peerage
2 CONT
2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Robert Lumsden:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p33143.htm#i331422
