2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/126209968/caleb-forbes
2 CONT
2 CONT Aged 57 years, the son of John Forbes and Constant Mitchell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Caleb married 30 June 1681 in Norwich, New London County, Connecticut to SARAH GAGER, born February 1651 in New London, and died about 1702, age 50 years. Sarah was a daughter of John Gager. John was born 25 May 1620 in Little Wal
2 CONC dingfield, Suffolk County England and died 10 Dec 1703 in Norwich, New London, Connecticut, age 83, the son of William Gager (1590/2 Eng-1630 MA), a Surgeon. John Gager married before 1647 in England to Elizabeth Gore (1618- )
2 CONT
2 CONT Caleb Fobes was a Constable on the east side of Norwich, Connecticut in 1684-85; First Deacon in Church of Preston; Selectman; Town Treasurer; Committee on Land and Highways; was a signer of the Preston, Connecticut petition to th
2 CONC e Legislature for incorporation of the town in October 1686 and named among the fifteen landholders on the Plantation Act, dated 15 January 1686, on record at Preston. He was a Connecticut volunteer in the Narragansett Campaign of
2 CONC  King Philip's [Indian] War and an original proprietor of Voluntown, Ct. At the time of his death, his estate was valued at $3,125.
2 CONT
2 CONT A qualifying ancestor for the Society of Colonial Wars.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Caleb Fobes and Sarah Gager:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Sarah Fobes (1684-1759).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Caleb Fobes (ii) (1689-1728).
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Mary Fobes (1694- ).
