2 CONT Catherine Newcomen married, firstly, Sir Alexander Stewart, 2nd Bt., son of Sir William Stewart, 1st Bt..[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married, secondly, Arthur Forbes, 1st Earl of Granard, son of Sir Arthur Forbes, 1st Bt. and Jane Lauder, circa 1655.[3] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 8 December 1714 at Dublin, County Dublin, Ireland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of Sir Robert Newcomen, 4th Bt. and Anne Boleyn.[1] 
2 CONT *Her married name became Stewart. 
2 CONT *From circa 1655, her married name became Forbes.[1] As a result of her marriage, Catherine Newcomen was styled as Viscountess of Granard on 22 November 1675. As a result of her marriage, Catherine Newcomen was styled as Countess 
