1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Arthur Forbes:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p5564.htm#i55636
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Forbes, 2nd Earl of Granard [1]
2 CONT *M, #55636, 
2 CONT *b. circa 1656, 
2 CONT *d. 24 August 1734
2 CONT *Last Edited=10 Apr 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Forbes, 2nd Earl of Granard was born circa 1656.[2] He was the son of Arthur Forbes, 1st Earl of Granard and Catherine Newcomen.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Rawdon, daughter of Sir George Rawdon, 1st Bt. and Hon. Dorothy Conway, in 1678.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 24 August 1734 at Symon's Court, County Dublin, Ireland.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Career:
2 CONT *He fought in the Battle of Saspach.[1] He fought in the Battle of Buda in 1686.[1] 
2 CONT *He was Colonel of the 18th Foot between 1686 and 1688.[1] 
2 CONT *He was imprisoned in the Tower of London.[1] 
2 CONT *He succeeded to the title of 2nd Earl of Granard [I., 1684] in 1695.[1] He succeeded to the title of 3rd Baronet Forbes, of Castle Forbes, Co. Longford, Ireland [N.S., 1628] in 1695.[1] He succeeded to the title of 2nd Baron Clan
2 CONC ehugh, co. Longford [I., 1675] in 1695.[1] He succeeded to the title of 2nd Viscount of Granard, co. Longford [I., 1675] in 1695.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Arthur Forbes, 2nd Earl of Granard and Mary Rawdon
2 CONT *1. Lady Jane Forbes+[1] d. Oct 1760
2 CONT *2. Lady Dorothy Forbes [1] d. 17 May 1779
2 CONT *3. unknown son Forbes [1]
2 CONT *4. unknown son Forbes [1]
2 CONT *5. Vice-Admiral George Forbes, 3rd Earl of Granard+[1] b. 21 Oct 1685, d. 29 Oct 1765
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 2, page 1628. Hereinafter cited as Burke's 
2 CONC Peerage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT *2. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VI, page 55. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
