1 OCCU Chief administrative officer (Finnish: Kamreeri) in the court of Count Brahe (from 1660 onward)., Chief administrative officer in the court of Count Brahe
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mårten Hansson Hörling was born in Turku, Finland, in 1623. He died in Stockholm, Sweden, on June 27, 1683. He was a son of a merchant and magistrate Hans Hörnigk (died on July 19, 1635) from Turku and Geska Hansdo
2 CONC tter Henning, a daughter of a printing house owner in Turku.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mårten completed his matriculation examination in Tartu, Estonia, on July 2, 1639. He continued studies in Turku in 1640–1641 and graduated in Tartu on April 4, 1642.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1643 onward, Mårten served in the court of Count Per Brahe the Younger (Feb. 18, 1602 – Sept. 2, 1680), who was a Privy Councillor from 1630, Governor-general of Finland from 1637, and Lord High Steward from 1640. From 1660 o
2 CONC nward, Mårten served as the chief administrative officer in the court of Count Brahe.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Sources and more information (in Finnish and Swedish):  http://helsinki.fi/ylioppilasmatrikkeli/henkilo.php?id=139
