1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In an email message dated 4 Sep 2007 Jens Anker sent the following:   (Translation of letter of 10 January, 1985 from Jan Fredrik Anker Solem)
2 CONT
2 CONT Else Marie Holm...says that Olof Eriksson (father of Erich Olofsson Ancker) cannot be seen to have taken out "borgerskap" (license to become a merchant) in Göteborg, and this indicates that his father  has already belonged to the 
2 CONC city's "borgerskap".  No doubt, one did not need to apply for "borgerskap" if one's father already had "borgerskap"
2 CONT
2 CONT Erik Bothvidsson, Olof's hypothetical father, is mentioned in 1639 as a "borger"(citizen, licenced merchant) in Göteborg,  He is spoken of as a "murmester" (master bricklayer)...
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Göteborg stads borgare längd 1621 - 1864 / published by Erland Långström - Göteborg, 1926.
