1 OCCU 3rd Baron of Ochiltree
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He did not marry his mother as was previously shown in Geni. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Wikipedia contributors. "<em>[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Stuart,_1st_Baron_Castle_Stuart Andrew Stuart, 1st Baron Castle Stuart]</em>." Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. also known as  3rd  Baron Ochiltree
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biographical notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1594 he took part in the Raid of Leith and, in 1597, became Warden of the West Marches. In 1608 he gave a dinner on board his ship for all the Hebridean chiefs, except Macleod and Macnell who mistrusted him, then kidnapped them
2 CONC  and made them the King's prisoners. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1611 because of pecuniary embarrassment, he sold and resigned the Lordship of Ochiltree to his nearest heir male in Scotland and emigrated to Ireland. On 7 November 1619, as Baron Castle Stuart, he was created an Irish peer. He
2 CONC  died in January 1628.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stuart-1843
2 CONT * http://www.thepeerage.com/p515.htm#i5144
2 CONT * http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00042741&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Stewart family citations regarding the Andrew Stewart 1st Baron of CastleStewart, N. Ireland say his grandson, George Stewart bc1625 in Scotland died in Termon, County Donegal, far north of Ireland and Ulster. He was called George
2 CONC  Stewart of Termon. At least three lines of Andrew's family immigrated to Pennsylvania: FIRST, George bc1685 to Donegal Township, Lancaster County before 1730 & then purchased property in Paxtang/S. Hanover Twp, SECOND, Andrew b16
2 CONC 98 to Paxtang Twp., Lancaster Co.in the 1730's, THIRD, Archibald b1695 to Chester Co., PA then moved to Paxtang Twp, Lancaster Co. by 1735. Two other siblings of Archibald settled in Augusta Co., Virginia and many lines of this fa
2 CONC mily remained in Virginia for generations. George Stewart of Termon, Donegal, Ireland bc1625, the first of this family line to live in Donegal, far northern part of Ireland/Ulster, was the grandfather of the FIRST to emigrate, and
2 CONC  great uncle of the SECOND & THIRD AND THOSE WHO ENDED UP IN VIRGINIA(one was Rebecca Stewart who married John McClung). Before Andrew Stewart Baron of CastleStewart, they came from the Stewarts of Ochiltree, Scotland. The family 
2 CONC line from Ochiltree to Donegal, Ireland/Ulster, from Andrew Stewart to George Stewart is given in citations in the Stewart family trees. Their fourth cousins, also coming from Andrew Stewart, Master of Ochiltree, Scotland, emigrat
2 CONC ed as well to Paxtang/S. Hanover/Drumore Townships, Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, two in 1735 and the other siblings before 1730. They were Samuel and Lazarus Stewart from Dromore, County Down, Ireland/Ulster(Drumore was "named 
2 CONC after Dromore (Irish: Droim Mór), County Down, Ireland, with which it has been twinned since 1996." from Wkipedia: Drumore). Samuel was one of the early settlers of Drumore Township, Lancaster, Pennsylvania, and later he moved up 
2 CONC to Paxtang/S. Hanover, Harrisburg. Lazarus settled in S. Hanover Township, Lancaster, PA very near the present-day Harrisburg, capital of Pennsylvania. Lazarus started the Old Hanover Presbyterian Church and was in the historic Pa
2 CONC xtang Presbyterian Church by 1729 when they obtained their first pastor. Right in the middle between Old Hanover, Paxtang churches and Drumore Church was the earliest church and considered the "mother" church located in Donegal To
2 CONC wnship, Lancaster, PA. That was where George Stewart of the Stewart family settled after he immigrated from Donegal, Ireland/Ulster in the 1720's.
2 CONT --------------------
