1 NOTE Considered to be the greatest Reformer in the history of Scotland. In 1560 he was appointed minister of the Church of St. Giles. He was buried there by the Earl of Mortoun.
2 CONT His most famous book, "The History of the Reformation of Scotland" is reknown with John's striving toward that effort.
2 CONT The Earl stated at his burial, "Here lyeth a man who in his life never feared the face of man, who hath been often threatened with dgger, but yet hath ended his dayes in peace and honor."
