1 CONC into a hail and free barony, "cum furca, fossa, pitt et gallous", &c, to be called the barony of O'Neill in all time coming. He married Elizabeth, sister of Panter of Newmanswells, near Montrose, secretary of state to James IV, an
1 CONC d had a son, Patrick of O'Neil Corse, infeft in 1554.”
