1 CONT !Lt. WILLIAM FOBES, son of John Fobes and Constant Mitchell; born probably Bridgewater, Mass., 1649 (6); married "the man to whom her father objected in his will". Little Compton, Rhode Island, 1678, Elizabeth Southworth, (daughte
1 CONC r of Constant Southworth and Elizabeth Collier), who was born ca. 1654 in Plymouth and who died 1681 (also referred to as Elizabeth Collier (Southworth & Elizabeth (Collier) Fobes --possible confusion between her and her mother); 
1 CONC married second about 1682, Martha Pabodie (Peabody) , (widow of Samuel Seabury and daughter of William Pabodie and Elizabeth Alden), who was born Durbury., Mass., 25 February 1650 and who died Little Compton, Rhode Island, 25 Janu
1 CONC ary 1712; he was LT COMMISSARY, in CAPT CHURCH'S 3RD EXPEDITION in KING PHILLIP'S WAR; ran a ferry from Little Compton to Newport in that part which is now  Middletown ; children Baptized in United Congregational Church of Little 
1 CONC Compton, R.I.; he died Seconnet (Little Compton), Rhode Island, 6 November 1712; no further FOBES name descendents, all girls; buriel Old Commons Cemetary, Little Compton, Rhode Island.
